1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:10,395
One morning in April 1973, an engineer stops on a New York sidewalk. He is on his way to a press conference, but first he wants to test something.

2
00:00:10,595 --> 00:00:19,928
He raises a device the size of a brick and dials a number. People turn around. Nobody had ever seen someone talking on a phone right in the middle of the street.

3
00:00:20,128 --> 00:00:28,210
Who is he calling? Not his mother or his boss. He calls Joel Engel, the head of the rival team. Remember that name.

4
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:32,013
The very first cell phone call was made to show off.

5
00:00:32,563 --> 00:00:40,868
Today there are more mobile lines than people on the planet. This is the story of the phone in your pocket. And how it works.
